WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.113
Today your child takes a sentence apart. Who is it about? What did they do? And where?

2
00:00:05.563 --> 00:00:08.142
Watch first. Then do the same with your child.

3
00:00:08.642 --> 00:00:10.757
Your child reads the sentence out loud.

4
00:00:11.157 --> 00:00:12.471
The hen sat on the bed.

5
00:00:13.171 --> 00:00:17.774
Under it are three boxes. Point to the first one, and ask: who is it about?

6
00:00:18.224 --> 00:00:20.369
Point to the middle one. What did they do?

7
00:00:20.819 --> 00:00:22.299
And the last one. Where?

8
00:00:22.749 --> 00:00:25.334
Your child circles one answer in each box.

9
00:00:25.784 --> 00:00:33.151
The first and the last box show the same two pictures. So your child has to know which one did it, and which one is the place.

10
00:00:33.601 --> 00:00:40.578
Your child cannot read the three question words yet. That is fine. The boxes keep the same order in every row.

11
00:00:41.028 --> 00:00:45.687
Job two is for your child alone. Three sentences, three boxes each.

12
00:00:46.137 --> 00:00:50.240
At the end, your child reads one sentence to you. Ask who, and where.

13
00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:54.457
In any book this week, try the same three questions after a page.
